Title: "The Fire Inside"
Raghav trusted him completely.
They had built everything together plans, work, dreams. Raghav never questioned him, never doubted him.
Until the day everything broke.
The truth came quietly. A deal made behind his back. Words twisted. Trust used like a tool.
At first, Raghav didn't believe it.
Then came the anger.
It burned fast.
Hot. Loud. Consuming.
He wanted to confront him, to shout, to break something the way he felt broken inside.
But instead, he walked away.
That night, the anger stayed. It sat heavy in his chest, asking to be released.
Days passed.
Raghav realized something slowly the betrayal hurt, but the anger was hurting him more.
So he chose something harder.
He didn't forgive immediately.
He didn't forget.
But he stopped feeding the fire.
He worked. He grew. He became stronger in silence.
And one day, the anger wasn't there anymore.
Just a quiet understanding:
Betrayal can light a fire inside you.
But you decide whether it burns you... or builds you.
